    "api_info" : {
      "title" : "Make Secured Http ",
      "description" : "* `url` — Specifies the target API endpoint where the HTTP request will be sent.\n* `headers` — Contains HTTP header key-value pairs used for authentication, content type, and additional request metadata.\n* `method` — Defines the HTTP operation type to be executed, such as GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, or PATCH.\n* `payload` *(inside payload)* — Represents the request body data that will be transmitted to the target API.\n* `authorizationType` — Determines which authentication mechanism should be applied while processing the request.\n* `urlParameters` — Holds dynamic path parameters or query parameters used to construct the final request URL.\n* `formData` — Stores multipart/form-data content typically used for file uploads and form submissions.\n* `settings` — Configuration object that controls request execution behavior and runtime options.\n* `sslValidation` — Enables or disables SSL certificate verification for HTTPS requests.\n* `responseAsInputStream` — Controls whether the API response should be returned as a stream instead of parsed content.\n* `requestTimeout` — Specifies the maximum duration the system should wait before terminating the request due to timeout.\n* `credentialId` — Unique identifier used to retrieve stored authentication credentials for secured API access.\n"
    },
